# BestoDine — frontend environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit the real `.env`.
#
# ⚠️  EVERY `VITE_*` VARIABLE IS COMPILED INTO THE PUBLIC JS BUNDLE.
#     Anyone can read these in DevTools. Only ever put values here that
#     are safe to publish. API keys that cost money (maps, payments,
#     mail) belong in Backend/.env behind a server endpoint — never
#     here.

# Backend API base, e.g. http://localhost:5000/api/v1
#
# Testing on a phone (same Wi-Fi): keep http://localhost:5000/api/v1.
# When the app is opened from another device (http://192.168.x.x:5173 —
# the dev server listens on the LAN via `vite --host`), the frontend
# automatically swaps a localhost/127.0.0.1 API host for the page's own
# hostname, keeping protocol, port and path (utils/apiOrigin.js). The
# socket.io URL and /uploads image URLs follow the same rule. The backend
# accepts LAN origins in development (CORS_ALLOW_LAN, default on in dev).
VITE_API_URL=

# ─── Google Sign-In ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The OAuth 2.0 *Web application* client ID. Must be the SAME value as
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in Backend/.env — the browser presents it, the server
# checks tokens were minted for it, and a mismatch rejects every login.
#
# Safe to expose: a client ID is public by design. There is no client
# secret in this integration at all (see Backend/.env.example).
#
# Leave blank to disable Google Sign-In — the button then renders
# nothing rather than appearing and failing.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ─── Marketing site (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# When set, the staff login shows a "Request a demo" link pointing at
# ${VITE_MARKETING_URL}/request-demo. Leave blank until the marketing
# site is deployed, or the link 404s on this app.
VITE_MARKETING_URL=

# ─── Public app URL (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Pins the host baked into customer links and table QR codes, e.g.
# https://app.example.com. Leave blank to use the current browser origin.
# If the admin browses on http://localhost:5173 and this is blank, table
# QR codes point at localhost and phones cannot open them — the QR modal
# warns and lets the admin set a per-browser QR base URL instead
# (e.g. http://192.168.1.24:5173). For LAN testing you can also set
# VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://<your-LAN-IP>:5173 here.
VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL=
